Version 0.1 -- 2026-08-10

    First public release.

  Features

    * Many functions to deal with the reading of Nintendo 64 Zelda ROMs:
      detection of DMADATA in ROMs, reading out MAKEROM headers, reading and
      modifying DMADATA.
    * Recalculation of Nintendo 64 ROM check codes across all CIC-NUS chips:
      the 6101, 6102, 6103, 6105, 6106 and their equivalents.
    * Writing of ROM headers and DMADATA.
    * Utility functions for getting information about entries in the DMADATA.
    * Introduction of the zelda64 manifest file format.

  Utilities

    * Two tools ship as part of this release, `compress` and `decompress`,
      which can be found in the utils folder.
    * A fast decompressor that can create a manifest file to turn the
      decompressed ROM back into the compressed ROM.
    * A highly compatible compressor that can create compressed ROMs that are
      byte exact with Nintendo's own tooling.
    * Uses libyaz0 version 0.2 for decompression and compression of ROM files.

  Correctness

    * Special care was taken to make sure that the library and utilities are
      highly compatible with existing tools.
    * Library and tools were tested against official, retail ROMs of Ocarina
      of Time and Majora's Mask for correctness, matching Nintendo's output
      exactly.

  Known Limitation

    * While decompression is fast (usually around 100 milliseconds),
      compression is currently rather slow, as `libzelda64-utils` delayed
      caching to version 0.2.
    * ABI or API stability is not yet guaranteed.
